{# Light, dark, or whatever the machine is set to.

   Three buttons rather than the currency switcher's trigger-and-panel, because
   there are three options and they fit: a panel would hide the current state
   behind a click, and the state is the only thing worth showing.

   `System` is the default and is not the same as picking light. A reader on
   that setting follows their machine, so a laptop that dims at sunset dims this
   with it -- which is the reason the feature was asked for.

   No server involvement and no cookie. The choice is per-browser and affects
   nothing anybody else sees, so it lives in localStorage and the markup ships
   the same for everyone. That also means this renders with `System` pressed on
   every page and the script corrects it, which is why the buttons carry
   `aria-pressed` rather than `aria-current`: nothing here is a destination. #}
<div class="theme js-theme" role="group" aria-label="Colour theme">
    <button type="button" class="theme__option is-on" data-theme-choice="system" aria-pressed="true">
        <i class="fas fa-circle-half-stroke" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Match system</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="theme__option" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="false">
        <i class="fas fa-sun" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Light</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="theme__option" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="false">
        <i class="fas fa-moon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Dark</span>
    </button>
</div>
